sful gate completion, `gh pr list -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --head <branch>` returns the newly opened PR.\\n5. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/skills/gate-push/` passes with no errors.\\n6. `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` Skills Overview lists `/dh:gate-push` with an accurate one-line description.\\n7. The branch\u2192issue resolution algorithm is documented in SKILL.md (slug derivation from branch name, backlog_list lookup strategy, fallback path when no match found).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:complete-implementation \u2014 quality gates and push/PR logic to delegate to |\\n| Skill | /dh:work-backlog-item \u2014 branch\u2192issue resolution patterns (parser, item_ref format) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Final Step: Commit and Push section (lines 887-905) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Recursive Follow-up Handling Step 2 slug derivation algorithm |\\n| Research | `research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md` \u2014 semantic model for branch-as-gate-trigger |\\n| Related item | #2104 \u2014 Run /complete-implementation quality gates in an isolated worktree (P1, open) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (can be built independently of any other open backlog item)\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n- Related: #2104 (Run /complete-implementation quality gates in an isolated worktree, P1) \u2014 if #2104 ships first, gate-push should delegate to the worktree-isolated version of complete-implementation. The two items are independent but ideally gate-push is implemented after or alongside #2104.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 one new SKILL.md document (~150-200 lines) defining the branch\u2192issue resolution algorithm, invocation flow, fallback behavior, and frontmatter. No Python code changes. The primary design work is the resolution algorithm (branch name \u2192 slug \u2192 backlog_list lookup) and the fallback interaction pattern. Follows existing patterns established in work-backlog-item's parser. Estimated: 1-2 hours of focused implementation work.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- None identified \u2014 gate-push is a new entry point, not a modification of existing interfaces.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 invoked by gate-push as a sub-skill; no interface change required, consumed as-is\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/gate-push/SKILL.md` \u2014 new skill file to be created; defines the branch\u2192issue resolution algorithm and gates invocation\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 auto-discovery handles new skills in `skills/` directory; no explicit update required\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: NOT_APPLICABLE\\n\\nNo existing implementation of gate-push exists in the codebase. This is a net-new skill with no prior implementation to assess alignment against.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Skills Overview section lists all dh skills; needs a new entry for `/dh:gate-push` with description\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] gate-push SKILL.md created with correct frontmatter (user-invocable: true, argument-hint: <branch-name>)\\n- [ ] Branch\u2192issue resolution algorithm documented in SKILL.md\\n- [ ] Fallback behavior (no match found \u2192 prompt for issue number) documented\\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md Skills Overview updated with gate-push entry\\n- [ ] Skill validated with `uvx skilllint@latest check`\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n**Rationale**: This is a new capability with no existing analogue in the codebase. It requires designing a branch\u2192issue resolution algorithm, defining fallback behavior, and specifying how to bridge a git concept (branch name) to a SAM concept (issue number or plan path). None of these design questions have existing patterns to follow exactly \u2014 they require framing before implementation.\\n**Analysis Method**: design-framing\\n**Scenario Target**: developer invokes `/dh:gate-push feature/foo` \u2192 skill resolves linked issue, runs complete-implementation gates, opens PR on success\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/gate-push/` \u2014 new skill directory (to create)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 existing quality-gate skill, consumed by gate-push\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 plugin meta-docs listing all skills\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 plugin manifest with auto-discovery\\n- `research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md` \u2014 source reference for the branch-push gate pattern\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nToday the developer must explicitly run `/dh:complete-implementation {plan-or-issue}` to invoke quality gates; only then are they pushed and a PR opened. There is no single command that takes a branch name and executes the equivalent of \\\"validate this branch via gates, push if clean, open PR.\\\" The closest existing command is `/dh:work-backlog-item` which expects an issue title, and `/dh:complete-implementation` which expects a plan path or issue number \u2014 neither maps the human-natural verb \\\"push this branch\\\" to the gate pipeline.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new user-invocable skill `plugins/development-harness/skills/gate-push/SKILL.md` accepts a branch name as its argument. It locates the linked backlog issue (via branch-name \u2192 slug \u2192 backlog match), invokes `/dh:complete-implementation` with the resolved issue/plan, and on success completes the existing push+PR step. Behaviour matches `git push no-mistakes <branch>` semantically: one verb, full gate pipeline, automatic PR. SKILL.md describes the branch\u2192issue resolution algorithm and what happens when no match is found (fall back to prompting the developer for the issue number).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `/dh:gate-push feature/foo` on a branch with a linked backlog issue. The run dispatches the same 6 quality-gate phases as `/dh:complete-implementation`. On success, `gh pr list -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --head feature/foo` returns the freshly opened PR. New skill file `plugins/development-harness/skills/gate-push/SKILL.md` exists. The frontmatter has `user-invocable: true` and `argument-hint: <branch-name>`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: ./research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 git push no-mistakes &lt;branch&gt; as the gate trigger.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"52bd29b0765ff1c4cb74ec494c30611aa81ff7ace0956699719cab1b75f983a4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCbT0w\"}"}